.TH LASTWAVE 1 "September 2026" "lastwave 0.5.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lastwave \- LastWave-inspired YouTube Music TUI player for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lastwave
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lastwave
is a terminal user interface for YouTube Music and local audio. It searches
YouTube Music directly through the public InnerTube API, resolves audio streams
without a browser or cookies, and plays them through
.BR mpv (1).
It supports a local file library, playlists, a deep-bass EQ preset, persistent
session resume, MPRIS desktop integration, and full-screen terminal album art
(half-block rendering, or the kitty graphics protocol when running under
kitty).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-volume " " \fIVOLUME\fR
Start volume (0\(en150), overrides the value in the configuration file.
.TP
.B \-\-mpv\-path \fIPATH\fR
Path to the
.B mpv
binary to use for playback.
.TP
.B \-\-resume
Restore the previous session (queue, position, history) on startup. The default
is controlled by the
.B resume
configuration option.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-resume
Start fresh, ignoring any saved session. Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-resume .
.TP
.B \-\-play \fIARG\fR
Start playback immediately. If
.I ARG
is an existing local file path it is enqueued and played directly; otherwise it
is treated as a search query and the first playable result is autoplayed.
Implies
.BR \-\-no\-resume .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The configuration file
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/lastwave/config.toml
(typically
.BR ~/.config/lastwave/config.toml )
is created with default values on first run. Supported keys:
.TP
.B volume
Start volume for mpv, 0\(en150 (integer).
.TP
.B mpv_path
Path to the mpv binary (string).
.TP
.B cache_dir
Directory for cached album art (string path).
.TP
.B autoplay
Autoplay the next track when the current one ends (boolean).
.TP
.B codec
Preferred audio codec: "best", "opus", or "aac" (string).
.TP
.B local_dirs
List of directories scanned for local audio files (array of paths).
.TP
.B resume
Restore the previous queue/position/history on startup (boolean, default true).
.TP
.B backend
Playback engine: "mpv" (default) or "mpd" (string).
.TP
.B mpd.socket
[mpd] Unix socket path, or mpd.host/mpd.port for a network daemon (string).
.TP
.B mpd.host, mpd.port, mpd.password
[mpd] MPD connection settings (string/integer/string).
.TP
.B eq
[eq] Equalizer settings; see presets in the generated file.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.config/lastwave/config.toml
Configuration file.
.TP
.B ~/.config/lastwave/session.json
Saved session state (queue, search history, playback position).
.TP
.B ~/.cache/lastwave/art
Cached album art thumbnails.
.TP
.B ~/.config/lastwave/playlists
Saved playlists.
.TP
.B ~/.config/lastwave/lastwave.lock
Single-instance lock file (removed on clean exit).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B KITTY_WINDOW_ID, TERM
When running under kitty (or when TERM is "xterm-kitty"), album art is rendered
using the kitty graphics protocol. Otherwise half-block art is used.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME, XDG_CACHE_HOME
Base directories for configuration and cache files.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B q
Quit.
.TP
.B ? 
Help/key map overlay.
.TP
.B / and s
Search.
.TP
.B Alt+l
Like/unlike the current track.
.TP
.B Alt+P
Manage playlists.
.TP
.B Alt+o, Alt+t
Queue view / add to queue.
.TP
.B Alt+u
Local file library browser.
.TP
.B Alt+n, Alt+p, Alt+e, Alt+x
Next track, previous track, EQ toggle, EQ panel.
.TP
.B Alt+r, Alt+z
Repeat mode, shuffle.
.TP
.B Alt+g
Go to artist/album of the current track.
.TP
.B Alt+a
Cycle mpv audio output device.
.TP
.B Alt+R
Start a radio from the current selection.
.TP
.B Alt+h
Search history.
.TP
.B space, j/k, Enter, Esc, Tab
Play/pause, navigation, select, back, cycle focus. Most other letters type
into the active input field.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
launch the player
.B lastwave
.TP
play a local file immediately
.B lastwave --play ~/Music/album.flac
.TP
search and autoplay
.B lastwave --play "Tame Impala The Less I Know The Better"
.TP
start at 80% volume without resuming
.B lastwave --volume 80 --no-resume
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B lastwave
exits 0 on success and nonzero on error (for example a missing mpv binary or an
unusable configuration file).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mpv (1),
.BR playerctl (1)
.PP
The full manual, key map, and configuration reference are available in the
project README.